# Why this rule exists

This project standardizes on PostgreSQL. Do not migrate to MongoDB or introduce other document databases.

# Rule

Always use PostgreSQL for database operations. Do not use MongoDB for new work; keep existing and new data access on PostgreSQL.

# Checklist

- Use PostgreSQL for database storage and queries.
- Do not add MongoDB (or other document-store) data layers or dependencies.
- Prefer PostgreSQL-native patterns (SQL, Prisma/Postgres, parameterized queries) over document-store APIs.

# Related technologies

- PostgreSQL
